      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\), we need to determine the smallest four-digit number and then find the smallest multiple of \\(33\\) that is greater than or equal to this number.\n\nFirst, identify the smallest four-digit number:\n\\[ 1000 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the smallest multiple of \\(33\\) that is greater than or equal to \\(1000\\). We do this by dividing \\(1000\\) by \\(33\\) and round up to the nearest whole number.\n\n\\[ \\frac{1000}{33} \\approx 30.303 \\]\n\nSince we need a whole number, we round \\(30.303\\) up to the next whole number, which is \\(31\\). Now, multiply \\(31\\) by \\(33\\) to find the smallest multiple of \\(33\\) that is greater than or equal to \\(1000\\):\n\\[ 31 \\times 33 = 1023 \\]\n\nThus, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1023} \\]",
