    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\), we need to identify the smallest four-digit number and then determine if it is divisible by \\(33\\). If it is not, we will find the next number that is divisible by \\(33\\).\n\nThe smallest four-digit number is \\(1000\\). We need to check if \\(1000\\) is divisible by \\(33\\). We can do this by performing the division:\n\n\\[ 1000 \\div 33 \\approx 30.303 \\]\n\nSince \\(1000\\) divided by \\(33\\) gives a quotient of approximately \\(30.303\\), the integer part of the quotient is \\(30\\). We then multiply \\(30\\) by \\(33\\) to find the largest multiple of \\(33\\) that is less than or equal to \\(1000\\):\n\n\\[ 30 \\times 33 = 990 \\]\n\nSince \\(990\\) is a four-digit number, it is the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\). To confirm, we can check the division of \\(1000\\) by \\(33\\):\n\n\\[ 1000 \\div 33 \\approx 30.303 \\]\n\nThis confirms that \\(1000\\) is not divisible by \\(33\\), so the smallest four-digit number divisible by \\(33\\) is the next multiple of \\(33\\) after \\(990\\), which is \\(33 \\times 31 = 1023\\).\n\nTherefore, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\) is \\(\\boxed{1023}\\).",
